    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No. 13 Burrow Road is a truly special period home, dating from 1895 and occupying an enviable position in one of Sutton’s most highly regarded and sought-after coastal addresses. Enjoying direct access to Burrow Beach, the property commands splendid views across Ireland’s Eye, Lambay Island and the coastline beyond Portmarnock. Its exceptional maritime setting, coupled with its wonderful sense of history and character, makes this a particularly rare and appealing home.\r\n\r\nHaving been cherished by the same family for many years, the property retains an abundance of its original charm and character. While the house would now benefit from some updating, many of its fine period features have been carefully maintained and lovingly preserved. The bright and tastefully presented interiors retain a wonderful sense of elegance, with numerous original features adding to the appeal. The impressive floor-to-ceiling height throughout the accommodation creates a superb feeling of volume and space.\r\n\r\nParticular features include original fireplaces, complemented by attractive ornate plasterwork. The combination of period detail, generous proportions and exceptional coastal setting gives No. 13 Burrow Road a unique and timeless quality.\r\n\r\nThe location is simply outstanding. Burrow Beach is quite literally on the doorstep, providing a wonderful amenity for swimming, walking and enjoying the coastline. Sutton Cross and Sutton DART station are within a short walk, while Howth Village and harbour are also close. There is an excellent selection of shops, cafés, restaurants and renowned coastal walks. There is also an excellent choice of primary and secondary schools in the surrounding area, together with a wide range of sporting and recreational amenities.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation briefly comprises a welcoming entrance porch leading to a fine reception hallway. There are two well-proportioned reception rooms off the hallway, together with a utility room and pantry. To the rear is the kitchen, which opens through to an extended sunroom overlooking the gardens.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, there are four bedrooms, including a principal bedroom with ensuite, together with a family bathroom.\r\n\r\nOutside, the property is approached via a private, hedgerow-lined gravel driveway leading to a lawned front garden. To the rear lies a glorious mature landscaped garden, predominantly laid in lawn and enjoying a wonderful sense of privacy. A particular highlight is the direct access from the garden onto Burrow Beach, creating an exceptionally rare connection between home and coast.\r\n\r\nNo. 13 Burrow Road represents a wonderful opportunity to acquire a much-loved period residence in an outstanding coastal setting. With its wealth of original features, generous accommodation, mature gardens and direct beach access, this is a property of considerable charm and distinction."
      },
